      "analysis_policy": "The complete family is trt1 versus ctrl and trt2 versus ctrl, with 10 original plants in each group. For each comparison use a two-sided unequal-variance Welch mean test, with the conventional Welch-Satterthwaite reference under stipulated independent-plant and approximately normal within-group working assumptions. Use Bonferroni across both comparisons at family alpha 0.05, allowing dependence from the shared control. A treatment qualifies for greater mean dry weight only when its observed treatment-minus-control difference is positive and its family-adjusted p-value is at most 0.05. The source does not fully specify a dry-weight unit; do not relabel grams. Neither the working assumptions nor a causal or representative population interpretation is established by these data.",
